  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In Fedora 5 (as well as 4) when attempting to create a resource with a prefix containing \":\", Fedora fails to create the resource if the prefix is not already known to the internal namespace registry. Including the prefix in the namespace prefix config file does not make a difference.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This seems counter to the intent of Fedora 5 to no longer use the internal Fedora/modeshape namespace registry in client interactions. Ideally, you would be able to create resources with prefixes, so long as they were not reserved, such as \"fcr:\".",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
