  "description": "<p>In Fedora 5 (as well as 4) when attempting to create a resource with a prefix containing \":\", Fedora fails to create the resource if the prefix is not already known to the internal namespace registry. Including the prefix in the namespace prefix config file does not make a difference.</p>\n\n<p>This seems counter to the intent of Fedora 5 to no longer use the internal Fedora/modeshape namespace registry in client interactions. Ideally, you would be able to create resources with prefixes, so long as they were not reserved, such as \"fcr:\".</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\ncurl -XPOST http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/ -H<span class=\"code-quote\">\"Slug: abc:123\"</span>\r\n</span>&lt; HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\r\nPrefix abc has not been registered\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p> </p>",
